5]\nL9: # Title:WMPO: World Model-based Policy Optimization for Vision-Language-Action Models\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Fangqi Zhu , cite6†Zhengyang Yan , cite7†Zicong Hong , cite8†Quanxin Shou , cite9†Xiao Ma , cite10†Song Guo L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled WMPO: World Model-based Policy Optimization for Vision-Language-Action Models, by Fangqi Zhu and 5 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite11†View PDF L16: > Abstract:Vision-Language-Action (VLA) models have shown strong potential for general-purpose robotic manipulation, but their reliance on expert demonstrations limits their ability to learn from failures and perform self-corrections. Reinforcement learning (RL) addresses these through self-improving interactions with the physical environment, but suffers from high sample complexity on real robots.\nL17: We introduce World-Model-based Policy Optimization (WMPO), a principled framework for on-policy VLA RL without interacting with the real environment. In contrast to widely used latent world models, WMPO focuses on pixel-based predictions that align the \"imagined\" trajectories with the VLA features pretrained with web-scale images. Crucially, WMPO enables the policy to perform on-policy GRPO that provides stronger performance than the often-used off-policy methods.\nL18: Extensive experiments in both simulation and real-robot settings demonstrate that WMPO (i) substantially improves sample efficiency, (ii) achieves stronger overall performance, (iii) exhibits emergent behaviors such as self-correction, and (iv) demonstrates robust generalization and lifelong learning capabilities.\nL19: Comments:  | project website: cite12†this https URL†wm-po.github.io L20: Subjects:  | Robotics (cs.RO); Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI)\nL21: Cite as:  | cite13†arXiv:2511.09515 [cs.RO]\nL22:    | (or cite14†arXiv:2511.09515v1 [cs.RO] for this version)\nL23:    | cite15†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2511.09515†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via